<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's short-term PHIBOR rates mostly higher.</title>
<headline>Manila's short-term PHIBOR rates mostly higher.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Short-term Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) were mostly higher on Wednesday in reponse to the higher overnight rates, while the rest were steady, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;Rates were higher at the short-end, signifying that banks are looking at a short-term aberration in interest rates,&quot; a trader said.</p>
<p>PHIBOR represents rates at which banks are willing to swap their pesos for dollars.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			  OCT 2		   OCT 1</p>
<p>    1 W		12  3/16		12  1/8</p>
<p>    2 W		12  1/16		12</p>
<p>    1 M		11 15/16		11 15/16</p>
<p>    2 M		11 13/16		11  3/4</p>
<p>    3 M		11  3/4		 11  3/4</p>
<p>    6 M		11 15/16		11 15/16</p>
<p>    12M		12			12</p>
<p>    VAL		3-Oct		   2-Oct</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom (632) 841-8937</p>
